1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,177
Welcome to the Authors Bureau Marketing Hub.

2
00:00:03,177 --> 00:00:07,408
This is where you review and manage the campaigns connected to each book.

3
00:00:07,408 --> 00:00:09,414
Start with Marketing Scope.

4
00:00:09,414 --> 00:00:14,257
If you have more than one book, choose Switch book and select the title you want to work on.

5
00:00:14,257 --> 00:00:18,763
Keep this selection in view before you review or activate anything.

6
00:00:18,763 --> 00:00:24,348
Every sequence, social post, and contact shown below follows this book selection.

7
00:00:24,348 --> 00:00:27,591
The Overview brings your campaign activity together.

8
00:00:27,591 --> 00:00:30,416
Each campaign has a clear status.

9
00:00:30,416 --> 00:00:34,049
Not Built means the content still needs to be created.

10
00:00:34,049 --> 00:00:36,458
Draft means it is ready for your review.

11
00:00:36,458 --> 00:00:39,973
Ready to Activate means the approved assets can be connected.

12
00:00:39,973 --> 00:00:46,315
Active means the campaign is currently available, and Pause lets you stop it without deleting the work.

13
00:00:46,315 --> 00:00:50,494
Open Sequences to review the emails connected to the selected book.

14
00:00:50,494 --> 00:00:54,739
Read the subject lines and message content before activation.

15
00:00:54,739 --> 00:00:58,828
You stay in control: reviewing a sequence does not send it.

16
00:00:58,828 --> 00:01:02,916
Activate only when the wording and sender settings are correct.

17
00:01:02,916 --> 00:01:07,890
The Social Calendar uses a copy-and-paste workflow, not automatic posting.

18
00:01:07,890 --> 00:01:13,593
Choose a post, set the date if needed, copy the caption, and download the graphic.

19
00:01:13,593 --> 00:01:19,361
Then open LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, or X and publish it yourself.

20
00:01:19,361 --> 00:01:23,645
When it is live, return here and mark the post as posted.

21
00:01:23,645 --> 00:01:28,632
This keeps your calendar accurate while you retain control of every social account.

22
00:01:28,632 --> 00:01:33,007
Contacts shows the readers and leads captured for the selected book.

23
00:01:33,007 --> 00:01:38,398
Use it to see who has entered your author journey and where each contact came from.

24
00:01:38,398 --> 00:01:41,367
Settings holds your email sender details.

25
00:01:41,367 --> 00:01:47,591
Confirm these before turning on an email sequence so replies and delivery details are correct.

26
00:01:47,591 --> 00:01:55,416
The safe routine is simple: select the book, review the assets, confirm the settings, and activate only when you are ready.

27
00:01:55,416 --> 00:01:56,770
Authors Bureau.

28
00:01:56,770 --> 00:01:58,736
Your Story is Your LIFE.

